  "limitations": [
    "Planned only. Resolve timer-only RequireReview versus whole-input mixed effects/global status and authorized continuation with reviewed examples. CORE-008 owns signed manual policy, ACCT-005 review composition, ACCT-006 financial reversal. Preserve applied components, exact held remainder, atomic resolution/no replay; mixed post-finish time/score needs explicit representation, never fake cap/unapplied. Next: owning contract, tests/review/red before implementation.",
    "Observed red comprises the reviewed 40-invocation run at f971df4a and the two-invocation focused rerun at 79e02053. These are separate runner observations with their original receipts. Correction 3 preserved the reviewed tests.",
    "Review covers the internal Qt owner, serial review transactions, durable journaling, exact retry, authority, bounded profile and additive v19 compatibility in synthetic SQLite. It establishes no production host composition, host reply eligibility or writer-profile adoption.",
    "The admitted C4 successor passed 41 feature and 1,444 companion invocations across 26 runners with no failures or skips. The separate focused authority probe and extracted SQLite projection checks passed. The standalone probe had one fixture-constructor shadowing warning.",
    "The integration preserves product and test source bytes. Ordinary Qt registration was locally checked with the admitted product binary under the generated registration and JUnit guard. Exact final-head hosted CI remains a separate gate.",
    "DB-01 remains partial. #294 owns host integration and no-reply, #750 owns shared-reader hardening, and #751 owns the source-derived allocation-failure case."
  ],
